  data: {
    LLM: "In Phase 1, throw away your low cards (Trash). Keep your Aces and 10s. Do not win tricks that contain low cards unless you have to (Phase 1 tricks go into your hand for Phase 2? Yes! You collect the trick). So, you want to win tricks with high cards inside them. Losing a trick means you don't get the cards. But you want high cards. So win big tricks.\n\nCounting Suits: In Phase 2, you must follow suit. If you have the only Spade left (the Ace), hold it until someone leads Spades, then crush them. If you have small cards in Phase 2, try to sneak them out early or on a new lead.\n\nThe 'Sacrifice': Sometimes in Phase 1, you let an opponent win a trick full of Queens if it means you can save your Ace for a trick full of Aces/Kings later. The quality of your Phase 2 hand is everything.",
    Player: "In Phase 1, throw away your low cards (Trash). Keep your Aces and 10s. Do not win tricks that contain low cards unless you have to (Phase 1 tricks go into your hand for Phase 2? Yes! You collect the trick). So, you want to win tricks with high cards inside them. Losing a trick means you don't get the cards. But you want high cards. So win big tricks.\n\nCounting Suits: In Phase 2, you must follow suit. If you have the only Spade left (the Ace), hold it until someone leads Spades, then crush them. If you have small cards in Phase 2, try to sneak them out early or on a new lead.\n\nThe 'Sacrifice': Sometimes in Phase 1, you let an opponent win a trick full of Queens if it means you can save your Ace for a trick full of Aces/Kings later. The quality of your Phase 2 hand is everything.",
